{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/450363-mad-wolves","id":450363,"title":"Mad wolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-20T06:30:55-07:00","id":450363,"title":"Mad wolves","content":"I was looking at the Gifts of Inspiration, and thought &quot;Lunatic Inspiration might be a handy one to put on a pack member as they'd be Inspired every day and at the end they'd get some message from Luna. I wonder how the Madness Condition works...&quot;<br /> <br /> The Madness Condition works off of Integrity, being as it otherwise usually comes when things fail breaking points. The ST gets to take away 10 - Integrity dice from you once per chapter.<br /> If a Werewolf has the Madness Condition (say, by having that Gift Facet used on her), do you just apply a 10 - Harmony modifier? That seems a little odd as 5 is supposed to be the sweet spot for werewolves. I guess it maybe makes a little sense as 10 Harmony represents someone who has a persistently repressed sense of the supernatural. But then again, they're really messed up people that will kill their neighborhood over tiny infractions like being there when the full moon rises...<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T06:49:47-07:00","id":450388,"title":"","content":"Note that you can only use Lunatic Inspiration on a human or Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> That said, it's still worth figuring out how Madness works for Uratha since there are other ways of getting it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T09:43:53-07:00","id":450532,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, it does say that it's just for humans and Wolf-Blooded. That's one of the few Facets of Inspiration that uses a roll, so I skipped right over the how-it's-used blurb to the Success bit.<br /> This brings up a few more questions. <br /> Are there other powers from other types of creatures that leave you with Madness?<br /> Is there a point in the book with suggestions on how to handle non-main character advancement? The Beats-Experience system is pretty well fleshed out for main characters, but it seems like it would lead to less-played characters getting left pretty far behind. I guess that could be something of a feature, but my question is really about whether there is advice from someone who has thought this through and tested it out somewhere. But there's a fair number of things that give away Beats to the people you're using your powers on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T10:40:20-07:00","id":450579,"title":"","content":"You mean like for NPCs? They gain Willpower instead of Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T11:55:47-07:00","id":450667,"title":"","content":"NPCs, sure, but also the Wolf-blooded and humans in the pack that get played sometimes. Do they advance at all? <br /> Also, is that in the book somewhere? I'm not doubting that you're right so much as hoping it's out there for people to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T11:41:55-07:00","id":458170,"title":"","content":"You could do:<br /> <br /> Harmony 5 = Integrity 10.<br /> Harmony 4/6 = Integrity 9.<br /> Harmony 3/7 = Integrity 8.<br /> Harmony 2/8 = Integrity 7.<br /> Harmony 1/9 = Integrity 6.<br /> Harmony 0/10 = Integrity 5.<br /> <br /> Or lower it by 2 each instead of 1. Or some other way. I would honestly just use it straight and say that the closer you are to the Spirit, the more prone to are to losses in human logic (which is what Madness is, sort of). And Harmony 5 may be a sweet spot for wolves, but this could just be one of the downsides of being balanced: less resistance to things that attack Integrity than someone to cleaves to the Flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T12:30:18-07:00","id":458253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/450363-mad-wolves?p=458170#post458170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would honestly just use it straight and say that the closer you are to the Spirit, the more prone to are to losses in human logic (which is what Madness is, sort of). And Harmony 5 may be a sweet spot for wolves, but this could just be one of the downsides of being balanced: less resistance to things that attack Integrity than someone to cleaves to the Flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty great solution, especially since going all in as Forsaken and taking a Lune as your Totem is supposed to lead to Madness...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T14:13:04-07:00","id":458340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/450363-mad-wolves?p=450667#post450667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NPCs, sure, but also the Wolf-blooded and humans in the pack that get played sometimes. Do they advance at all? <br /> Also, is that in the book somewhere? I'm not doubting that you're right so much as hoping it's out there for people to find.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's in a sidebar in GMC, but I don't remember exactly. I'll see if I can find it again.<br /> <br /> As for the side characters in the pack, I would let them gain Beats normally. They'll naturally advance a little slower than the main characters just because they're not involved in as much of the action, but I think that is probably fine. Might be tricky if you use group Beats though...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found it. GMC, page 180 under the heading Conditions on Storyteller Characters: &quot;Storyteller characters don\u2019t usually track Experiences the way the players\u2019 characters do. Any time a Storyteller character offered experience by a Condition, they simply regain a point of Willpower for use in the same scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, if you meant for the players' side characters... I *think* them advancing more slowly is a feature, not a bug, but I could see it causing problems with some groups, especially ones that use the Group Beats option... I don't have an easy answer to that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-26-2015, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T15:10:14-07:00","id":458376,"title":"","content":"Group Beats seems like it would make it easier to advance them along with everyone else since everyone advances at the same rate. Just make the Beat Pool, divide it by players, and give that to all characters.<br /> <br /> Or have them happen more slowly. I'll bring it up tonight with my group and see what they think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T16:06:59-07:00","id":458450,"title":"","content":"Just a random idea for the Group Beats issue: maybe give the side characters a Beat or two every time the main characters get an Experience? That way they still advance alongside the main characters, but obviously not as quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5299-trivialrealities","name":"trivialrealities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5299_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T04:01:15-07:00","id":458795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/450363-mad-wolves?p=458376#post458376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Group Beats seems like it would make it easier to advance them along with everyone else since everyone advances at the same rate. Just make the Beat Pool, divide it by players, and give that to all characters.<br /> <br /> Or have them happen more slowly. I'll bring it up tonight with my group and see what they think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm proud and impressed at all you STs who have the energy to track such minutiae. In my humble opinion, NPCs gain new abilities when I feel it's story appropriate. NPC packmates included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T04:38:00-07:00","id":458812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mother's Love</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/450363-mad-wolves?p=458795#post458795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm proud and impressed at all you STs who have the energy to track such minutiae. In my humble opinion, NPCs gain new abilities when I feel it's story appropriate. NPC packmates included.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! It's not something we've actually done yet, but I appreciate your encouraging tone!<br /> Does your group have any semi-NPCs? As in characters that the Storyteller keeps track of while everyone is being a werewolf but that players pick up when their wolf is off-screen? My group is planning to do that, and my main question/musing was on how to advance them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}